DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The jj00() and jj11() functions return Bessel functions of _x of  the  first
       kind  of  orders  0 and 1, respectively.  The jjnn() function returns the
       Bessel function of _x of the first kind of order _n.

       The jj00ff(), jj11ff(), and jjnnff(), functions are versions that take  and  re‐
       turn  _f_l_o_a_t values.  The jj00ll(), jj11ll(), and jjnnll() functions are versions
       that take and return _l_o_n_g _d_o_u_b_l_e values.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the appropriate Bessel value of  the
       first kind for _x.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is too large in magnitude, or the result underflows, a range error
       occurs, and the return value is 0.

